  "_notes": [
    "proof is a statement kind, not a separate class: it is a block with a heading and a body.",
    "inner_display has no wrapper of its own after normalisation: its rows join the enclosing display.",
    "grid keeps its delimiter because cases/array/matrix differ in the rendered delimiter, which is content.",
    "float and bibliography are dropped wholesale; the count is reported, not silently discarded.",
    "2026-11-18: the package environments that were most often unknown join their class -- tikz scope/overpic/pgfplots axis draw (diagram); multicols/mdframed/restatable/landscape/centering/spacing/keyword and the front/back matter wrappers keep their content (text_block); appendix and frontmatter are wrappers, not units.",
    "2026-11-18: the heads measured from unknown_envs after normalize (not from source counts): IEEEeqnarray/subeqn are displays, the nicematrix family is a grid, forest is a drawing.  math/title/author are not here -- they are handled as commands (\\begin{X} runs \\X).",
    "2026-11-18: the paralist family (compactitem/compactenum/compactdesc) is a list; it was the largest remaining unknown after the first five rules.",
    "2026-11-18: restatable removed from text_block -- normalize has a branch for it that the table entry made unreachable (audit J6, OPEN.md).",
    "2026-11-20: subarray moved from inner_display to grid -- inside a math group the inner_display rewrite broke the braces (C7, RULES.md)."
  ]
